# Netlify applies these to every response.
# Added 2026-09-15 after the security review: the site carried no
# headers beyond HSTS, so the dashboard could be framed by anyone.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# NOTE: a Content-Security-Policy was tried here on 2026-09-15 and had to
# be reverted within minutes. admin.html carries its whole application in
# an inline <script type="module">, and the CSP stopped it executing, so
# the dashboard rendered its sign-in form and nothing behind it worked.
# 'unsafe-inline' alone is not enough for that page.
#
# To reintroduce CSP safely, do it in this order:
#   1. Move the inline module out of admin.html into /js/admin.js
#   2. Then add: script-src 'self' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net
#   3. Test sign-in, the customer list and the composer BEFORE committing
# Until then the other headers below still close clickjacking and sniffing.

/admin.html
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/help.html
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

/unsubscribe
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
